      "source": [
        "# Logistic Regression – Diabetes Prediction\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "**Aim:** Train Logistic Regression for binary classification and plot the sigmoid function, decision boundary and ROC curve with AUC.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Author: Dr. Priya B. Pandharbale**\n",
        "\n",
        "Dataset: Pima Indians Diabetes (Kaggle). `Outcome`: 0 = Non-diabetic, 1 = Diabetic."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 1,
      "id": "2b0826d7",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2b0826d7"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
        "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, roc_curve, auc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "774dee51",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "774dee51"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 1. Load and prepare the data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 4,
      "id": "23dea1ec",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "23dea1ec",
        "outputId": "00cfbb48-8e4e-4f53-e484-e2ff604a9331"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "   Pregnancies  Glucose  BloodPressure  SkinThickness  Insulin   BMI  \\\n",
            "0            6      148             72             35        0  33.6   \n",
            "1            1       85             66             29        0  26.6   \n",
            "2            8      183             64              0        0  23.3   \n",
            "3            1       89             66             23       94  28.1   \n",
            "4            0      137             40             35      168  43.1   \n",
            "\n",
            "   DiabetesPedigreeFunction  Age  Outcome  \n",
            "0                     0.627   50        1  \n",
            "1                     0.351   31        0  \n",
            "2                     0.672   32        1  \n",
            "3                     0.167   21        0  \n",
            "4                     2.288   33        1  \n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "url = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/npradaschnor/Pima-Indians-Diabetes-Dataset/master/diabetes.csv\"\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(url)\n",
        "\n",
        "cols = [\"Glucose\", \"BloodPressure\", \"SkinThickness\", \"Insulin\", \"BMI\"]\n",
        "df[cols] = df[cols].replace(3, np.nan).fillna(df[cols].median())\n",
        "\n",
        "X = df.drop(\"Outcome\", axis=1)\n",
        "y = df[\"Outcome\"]\n",
        "print(df.head())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "717f693e",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "717f693e"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 2. Train the Logistic Regression model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 6,
      "id": "075da9f4",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "075da9f4",
        "outputId": "3dac39ed-1316-43f0-e028-5f7c8f2a3886"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Accuracy: 0.7662337662337663\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X, y, test_size=0.4, random_state=30, stratify=y)\n",
        "\n",
        "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
        "X_train = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
        "X_test = scaler.transform(X_test)\n",
        "\n",
        "model = LogisticRegression()\n",
        "model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "y_pred = model.predict(X_test)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Accuracy:\", accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "f887f209",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f887f209"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 3. Sigmoid function"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 7,
      "id": "18821263",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 472
        },
        "id": "18821263",
        "outputId": "d84730ac-84ec-4047-96fe-d660ee45891e"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "z = np.linspace(-30, 30, 200)\n",
        "plt.plot(z, 1 / (1 + np.exp(-z)))\n",
        "plt.title(\"Sigmoid Function\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Input\"); plt.ylabel(\"Probability\")\n",
        "plt.grid(); plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "685446a9",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "685446a9"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 4. Decision boundary\n",
        "\n",
        "Use Glucose and BMI to draw a simple 2D decision boundary. The main model above uses all eight features."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 8,
      "id": "8018cffb",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 507
        },
        "id": "8018cffb",
        "outputId": "308b122b-d74e-41a1-f205-90cf44f704c0"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stderr",
          "text": [
            "/usr/local/lib/python3.13/dist-packages/sklearn/utils/validation.py:2739: UserWarning: X does not have valid feature names, but StandardScaler was fitted with feature names\n",
            "  warnings.warn(\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "X2 = df[[\"Glucose\", \"BMI\"]]\n",
        "a, b = np.meshgrid(\n",
        "    np.arange(X2.Glucose.min(), X2.Glucose.max(), 3),\n",
        "    np.arange(X2.BMI.min(), X2.BMI.max(), 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "sc2 = StandardScaler()\n",
        "X2_scaled = sc2.fit_transform(X2)\n",
        "m2 = LogisticRegression().fit(X2_scaled, y)\n",
        "\n",
        "grid = sc2.transform(np.c_[a.ravel(), b.ravel()])\n",
        "pred = m2.predict(grid).reshape(a.shape)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.contourf(a, b, pred, alpha=0.5)\n",
        "plt.scatter(X2.Glucose, X2.BMI, c=y, edgecolors=\"k\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Glucose\"); plt.ylabel(\"BMI\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Decision Boundary\"); plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
