        "## Observations\n",
        "1. Logistic Regression predicts diabetic (1) or non-diabetic (0).\n",
        "2. The sigmoid function converts model scores into probabilities between 0 and 1.\n",
        "3. The decision boundary separates the two classes using Glucose and BMI.\n",
        "4. The ROC curve compares true-positive and false-positive rates at different thresholds.\n",
        "5. AUC closer to 1 indicates better separation of the two classes.\n",
        "\n",
